From: SaaiOS <os@saaios>
Subject: synaptics td4150: zero plen after continued_read; poll ATTN during 0x05

v019 since10: continued_read drains 13325-byte frames (drained=1) but
read_message still uses stale plen for check_padding → -EIO (rc=-5).
Salvage and stuck-assume-ok never fire; write_message times out 15s with
no IRQ reads during wait.

Root cause:
    After continued_read rem=0, payload_length stays 13325. total_length
    is computed before continued_read and check_padding indexes in.buf[13328]
    which is out of buffer → Incorrect message padding byte → -EIO.

Fix:
1. After continued_read with payload_fully_drained, set plen=0, recompute
   total_length, synthesize padding byte (same as plen==0 short path).
2. Salvage: accept syna_tcm_status_ok_drained() without requiring rc==0.
3. Stuck large-frame path: also trigger when payload_fully_drained.
4. ENABLE_REPORT wait: poll ATTN every 50ms and read_message proactively;
   reduce timeout 15s → 3s (salvage covers remainder).

Applies after syna-tcm-enable-report-plen-clear.patch.

--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics/td4150/synaptics_tcm_core.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics/td4150/synaptics_tcm_core.c
@@ -1150,12 +1150,23 @@ static int syna_tcm_read_message(struct syna_tcm_hcd *tcm_hcd,
 
 	LOCK_BUFFER(tcm_hcd->in);
 
+	/* continued_read may finish with rem=0 while header plen is still the
+	 * original multi-chunk size; check_padding uses total_length derived
+	 * from plen and would otherwise probe past in.buf → -EIO (rc=-5).
+	 */
+	if (tcm_hcd->payload_fully_drained)
+		tcm_hcd->payload_length = 0;
+
+	total_length = MESSAGE_HEADER_SIZE + tcm_hcd->payload_length + 1;
+
 	tcm_hcd->in.buf[0] = MESSAGE_MARKER;
 	tcm_hcd->in.buf[1] = tcm_hcd->status_report_code;
 	tcm_hcd->in.buf[2] = (unsigned char)tcm_hcd->payload_length;
 	tcm_hcd->in.buf[3] = (unsigned char)(tcm_hcd->payload_length >> 8);
 
+	if (tcm_hcd->payload_length == 0)
+		tcm_hcd->in.buf[total_length - 1] = MESSAGE_PADDING;
+
 check_padding:
 	if (tcm_hcd->in.buf[total_length - 1] != MESSAGE_PADDING) {
 		input_err(true, tcm_hcd->pdev->dev.parent,
@@ -1382,10 +1393,24 @@ static int syna_tcm_write_message(struct syna_tcm_hcd *tcm_hcd,
 
 	response_timeout_ms = RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_MS;
 	if (command == CMD_ENABLE_REPORT)
-		response_timeout_ms = 15000;
+		response_timeout_ms = 3000;
+
+	{
+		unsigned long deadline = jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(response_timeout_ms);
+
+		retval = 0;
+		while (time_before(jiffies, deadline)) {
+			unsigned long chunk = min(deadline - jiffies,
+					msecs_to_jiffies(50));
+
+			retval = wait_for_completion_timeout(&response_complete, chunk);
+			if (retval)
+				break;
+			if (command == CMD_ENABLE_REPORT &&
+					syna_tcm_attn_active(tcm_hcd))
+				syna_tcm_read_message(tcm_hcd, NULL, 0);
+		}
+	}
 
-	retval = wait_for_completion_timeout(&response_complete,
-					msecs_to_jiffies(response_timeout_ms));
 	if (retval == 0) {
 		input_err(true, tcm_hcd->pdev->dev.parent,
 			"Timed out waiting for response (command 0x%02x)\n", tcm_hcd->command);
@@ -2431,17 +2456,17 @@ int syna_tcm_enable_touch_report(struct syna_tcm_hcd *tcm_hcd)
 					tcm_hcd->payload_fully_drained ? 1 : 0);
 			}
 
-			if (rc == 0 && syna_tcm_status_ok_drained(tcm_hcd)) {
